**Report note agreement separately from blocker agreement.**

`N` is intentionally excluded from the blocking comparison, but `scorerAgreement` does not identify that scope or report `N` agreement. A future N-only difference can therefore be counted as agreement without being visible in the tally.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
 let agreed = 0;
+let noteAgreed = 0;
 const finalFlags = new Map<string, Flags>();
 for (const id of scorable) {
   const a = op.get(id)!, b = sa.get(id)!; assert.ok(a && b, `missing score for ${id}`);
   const same = blockers.every((f) => a[f] === b[f]);
+  if (a.N === b.N) noteAgreed++;
   if (same) { agreed++; assert.ok(!settled.has(id) || blockers.every((f) => settled.get(id)!.flags[f] === a[f])); finalFlags.set(id, a); }
   else { assert.ok(settled.has(id), `disagreement ${id} needs adjudication`); finalFlags.set(id, settled.get(id)!.flags); }
 }
...
-save("tally.json", { at: new Date().toISOString(), perCell: per, scorerAgreement: { scorable: scorable.length, agreed, adjudicated: scorable.length - agreed }, cells, totals, verdict, interpretation: plan.interpretation[verdict] });
+save("tally.json", { at: new Date().toISOString(), perCell: per, scorerAgreement: { scope: "blockers-only", scorable: scorable.length, agreed, adjudicated: scorable.length - agreed, noteAgreed, noteDisagreed: scorable.length - noteAgreed }, cells, totals, verdict, interpretation: plan.interpretation[verdict] });
```

</details>

**Track note agreement separately and adjudicate N-only differences.**

The scoring contract requires disagreements between the two scorers to be resolved, while `N` is excluded only from pass evaluation. `tally.mts` and `verify.mts` compare only `U`, `X`, `I`, and `F`, so an N-only difference can enter the `agreed` branch and select the operator’s `N` without adjudication. The current records contain no N-only difference, so this is a latent reporting and resolution gap.

Include `N` in the agreement decision, retain a separate blocker-agreement count, and report `noteAgreed` and `noteDisagreed`. Apply the same comparison in `verify.mts`.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
 let agreed = 0;
+let blockerAgreed = 0;
+let noteAgreed = 0;
 const finalFlags = new Map<string, Flags>();
 for (const id of scorable) {
   const a = op.get(id)!, b = sa.get(id)!; assert.ok(a && b, `missing score for ${id}`);
-  const same = blockers.every((f) => a[f] === b[f]);
+  const blockersSame = blockers.every((f) => a[f] === b[f]);
+  const notesSame = a.N === b.N;
+  if (blockersSame) blockerAgreed++;
+  if (notesSame) noteAgreed++;
+  const same = blockersSame && notesSame;
   if (same) { agreed++; assert.ok(!settled.has(id) || blockers.every((f) => settled.get(id)!.flags[f] === a[f])); finalFlags.set(id, a); }
   else { assert.ok(settled.has(id), `disagreement ${id} needs adjudication`); finalFlags.set(id, settled.get(id)!.flags); }
 }
...
-save("tally.json", { at: new Date().toISOString(), perCell: per, scorerAgreement: { scorable: scorable.length, agreed, adjudicated: scorable.length - agreed }, cells, totals, verdict, interpretation: plan.interpretation[verdict] });
+save("tally.json", { at: new Date().toISOString(), perCell: per, scorerAgreement: { scope: "all-flags", scorable: scorable.length, agreed, blockerAgreed, adjudicated: scorable.length - agreed, noteAgreed, noteDisagreed: scorable.length - noteAgreed }, cells, totals, verdict, interpretation: plan.interpretation[verdict] });
```

```diff
-  const same = blockers.every((f) => a[f] === b[f]); if (same) agreed++;
+  const same = blockers.every((f) => a[f] === b[f]) && a.N === b.N; if (same) agreed++;
```

